<title>USA: Perkin-Elmer Q3 oper shr higher.</title>
<headline>Perkin-Elmer Q3 oper shr higher.</headline>
<dateline>NORWALK, Conn 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>THE PERKIN-ELMER CORPORATION</p>
<p>CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>(Dollar amounts in millions except per share amounts)</p>
<p>							  Three months ended</p>
<p>							 March 31,</p>
<p>							 1997	     1996</p>
<p>Net revenues				   $  322.9	 $  299.1</p>
<p>Cost of sales				     157.1	    153.3</p>
<p>Gross margin					165.8	    145.8</p>
<p>Selling, general and administrative	  93.5	     86.0</p>
<p>Research, development and engineering	27.2	     25.7</p>
<p>Provision for restructured operations			   71.6</p>
<p>Acquired research and development	    25.4</p>
<p>Operating income (loss)			  19.7	   (37.5)</p>
<p>Interest income (expense), net		  1.4		0.2</p>
<p>Other expense, net				  0.1		0.1</p>
<p>Income (loss) before income taxes	    21.0	   (37.4)</p>
<p>Provision for income taxes		     10.6	   ( 1.4)</p>
<p>Net income (loss)			    $   10.4	$  (36.0)</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per share		$    0.23     $  (0.84)</p>
<p>Average common shares,</p>
<p>including dilutive equivalents	     44,850,000 43,426,000</p>
<p>							   Nine months ended</p>
<p>								March 31,</p>
<p>							 1997	     1996</p>
<p>Net revenues				   $  929.4	 $  857.5</p>
<p>Cost of sales				     465.4	    441.6</p>
<p>Gross margin					464.0	    415.9</p>
<p>Selling, general and administrative	 270.7	    249.4</p>
<p>Research, development and engineering	78.6	     76.8</p>
<p>Provision for restructured operations			   71.6</p>
<p>Acquired research and development	    25.4</p>
<p>Operating income				   89.3	     18.1</p>
<p>Gain on sale of investment		     37.4</p>
<p>Interest income (expense), net		  2.7	    (1.0)</p>
<p>Other expense, net				  0.2		2.1</p>
<p>Income before income taxes		    129.2	     15.0</p>
<p>Provision for income taxes		     35.5	     10.6</p>
<p>Net income				     $   93.7	$     4.4</p>
<p>Net income per share			 $   2.10	$    0.10</p>
<p>Average common shares,</p>
<p>including dilutive equivalents	 44,544,000     43,426,000</p>
<p>NOTE: The company reported a loss in the third quarter of fiscal 1996 after recording a charge for restructuring its Analytical Instruments Division.</p>
<p>Special items in fiscal 1997, in addition to the acquired research and development charge in the third quarter, included gains on the sale of equity investments in the first two quarters.</p>
<p>Including these items, third quarter operating income increased to $19.7 million, net income rose to $10.4 million, and earnings per share rose to $0.23.</p>
<p>Special restructuring charges for the same period the previous year brought the per share figure to a loss of $0.84.</p>
<p>Before the special items, third-quarter share profit was $0.80 compared to $0.60.</p>
<p>A currency translation reduced the current year third-quarter's earnings by $0.12 a share.</p>
